{
  "description": "full landing-page layout (header with mobile menu, hero, services, gallery, about, contact, footer); only if you need that structure",
  "entry": "index.html",
  "notes": "The layout and behavior are the starter; the design and content are yours. The look comes from the token block at the top of styles.css (colors, corner radius, fonts, borders) and two attributes on <body> (data-hero: blobs|grid|stripes|none, data-cards: grid|list). It starts neutral on purpose: set those tokens, the fonts and the shapes to suit what you are building, and restyle anything else the subject calls for. Replace ALL the placeholder copy in index.html with real writing for this subject, swap the gradient .tile blocks for real <img> tags with alt text, and add, remove or reorder sections freely (copy a <section class=\"section\"> block).",
  "theme_files": {
    "css": "styles.css"
  },
  "base_css": {
    "--step--1": "clamp(0.84rem, 0.82rem + 0.1vw, 0.9rem)",
